findings.proposal:
Make the substitution environment a field of S7 μ's ResolutionCtx (D7/C4): `type_params: TypeParamEnv { Declared(&HashSet<String>) | Bound(&Sigma) }`, derived by value (`ctx.with_bound(sigma).entering_alias(name)`). The single resolver entry D7 already creates (kinded and non-kinded collapse) then resolves alias bodies too. Hygiene ('a body must never see the use site's parameter scope') becomes the constructor `with_bound`, which replaces the set rather than extending it.

What dies:
- resolve_type_alias_expr_with_subst;
- resolve_parameterized_builtin_type_with_subst (D13's `subst: Option<&Subst>` parameter becomes this ctx field);
- the parity-note prose on resolve_entity_name_with_shadowing;
- the known-gap pin test, which turns green.

It would have prevented the #6477 applied-arm drop, #6259's four entity-body fixes and probe (c).

Coverage: extends #8643 (μ) and #8903 (S8-ο). Neither PRD collapses the alias-body resolver.

Introduce one relation computed once per eval in a lower module below the engine SCC (e.g. `auto_reach.rs`, importing deps/resolve_order primitives only, per S4 D13). The relation is `AutoReach { by_auto: BTreeMap<ValueCellId, Vec<Reacher>> }`, where `Reacher { source: ConstraintNodeId | ObjectiveTerm, via: ReadPath, drivable: Drivability }`. It is built from one declared edge policy, `ReachEdges { value_chains: bool, realization_chains: bool, through_optimized: Stop|Follow }`, and one spelling bridge (S3 ι #8704's InstancePath::structure_scope).

Every consumer becomes a query on it:
- layer 1's constraint admission (inside #6690's single builder);
- detect_underdetermined, as 'auto has no drivable reacher';
- compute_clusters' union pairs;
- constraints_reaching_auto, as 'reacher via a realization edge'.

Invariant: W_UNDERDETERMINED fires iff the problem builder admitted no constraint for that auto. This is enforced by construction, because both read the same `AutoReach`, and pinned by one cross-check test over the S4 υ #8877 differential fixtures.

What dies:
- auto_is_pinned_through_a_reader and its alias-oracle disjunct;
- the additive keying and seeding prose in cells_reaching;
