- the direct-only filters at engine_edit.rs 1732 and 4058, already slated by #6690.

It would have prevented all four #5467 fixes and #6649's wrong-warning half.

Coverage: the admission half (5)/(6) vs (1) is covered by solver-driver-parity β #6690 (one problem builder). S4 κ #8868 moves detect_underdetermined into detectors.rs and ν #8860 moves CellReadIndex to solver_problem.rs, both as pure moves, so (2), (3) and (4) are not covered. This extends #6690 and κ #8868.

Make the incremental serve a decision rather than an inherited obligation. Re-scope eval_cached to what its production consumer needs: `Engine::replay_last_eval(&CompiledModule) -> Option<EvalResult>`. It returns the retained EvalResult (values and diagnostics, with INV-EVAL-3 replay already stored per NodeCache) when the module's content_hash equals the last evaluated one, and None otherwise. The LSP falls through to eval() on None. Alternatively, the LSP can memoise its last diagnostics keyed by content_hash.

